B. Epic events:

(1) On the second day of war, the Tittira warriors, along with many others, were stationed at the right wing of the Krauñcāruṇavyūha (6. 46. 39; Krauñca 6. 47. 1) of the Pāṇḍavas (tittirāś caiva… ete janapadā rājan dakṣiṇaṁ pakṣam āśritāḥ) 6. 46. 50;

(2) On the eighth day of war, Irāvān confronted the cavalry of Śakuni and Hārdikya (Kṛtavarman) with his Tittira-bred horses which were swift, having the speed of wind, decorated with gold, provided with armour and wellequipped (ye cāpare tittirajā javanā vātaraṁhasaḥ) 6. 8
